{"tool_name":"messi","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:messi"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"messi","home":"https://github.com/doraadong/MESSI","license":"MIT","summary":"Identifying signaling genes in spatial single cell expression data.\n\nMESSI (Mixture of Experts for Spatial Signaling genes Identification) is a predictive framework to identify signaling genes active in cell-cell interaction. It jointly models gene interactions within and between cells, using the recently developed spatial single cell expression data. MESSI combines the ability to subdivide cell types with multi-task learning to accurately infer the expression of a set of response genes based on signaling genes and to provide useful biological insights about key signaling genes and cell subtypes.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:58:48Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-12T14:17:42.247063Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:messi","credit":[{"email":"zivbj@cs.cmu.edu","name":"Ziv Bar-Joseph","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Expression profile clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0313"},{"term":"Gene prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2454"},{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"}]}],"name":"MESSI","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa769","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.1101/2020.07.27.221465","type":["Preprint"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Zoology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3500"}]},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:messi/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":nul